[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943400999","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107139#issuecomment-2943400999","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107139","id":2943400999,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vcLwn","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-05T09:17:49Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T09:17:49Z","body":"> Lately we've been a bit more mindful about API breakage. It would be possible to expose a `[[deprecated]] void free` function in addition the `free_rid` to make the transition moother for modules. What do you think?\r\n\r\nYes this should definitely be added.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943400999/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943435323","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107139#issuecomment-2943435323","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107139","id":2943435323,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vcUI7","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-05T09:27:48Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T09:30:37Z","body":"~~Any concerns about changing the name of a `GDVIRTUAL` method in `PhysicsServer*DExtension`? I seem to recall there being some gotchas with godot-cpp and compatibility methods for `GDVIRTUAL` stuff.~~\r\n\r\nNevermind, I just realized it was already called `free_rid` on the extension side of things.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943435323/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"resolved"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943444849","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107139#issuecomment-2943444849","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107139","id":2943444849,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vcWdx","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-05T09:30:50Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T10:16:09Z","body":"@Ivorforce Sure, I'll add that in. It's easy to change this by editing the code of a module, ~~but the major advantage of that to me is it avoids conflicts with any currently in-flight PRs adding new calls to `free`, which should still be able to compile with such a compatibility method present.~~ Well, not anymore, it would fail the minimal CI build with deprecated disabled now that we have the `#ifndef` checks, so it seems not very useful to have this to me, but it's fine.\r\n\r\n@mihe It doesn't change that. The exposed GDVIRTUAL callback function, including in the extension classes, is already `_free_rid`. The old code is this:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nGDVIRTUAL1_REQUIRED(_free_rid, RID)\r\nvirtual void free(RID p_rid) override {\r\n\tGDVIRTUAL_CALL(_free_rid, p_rid);\r\n}\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943444849/reacti